 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty three\nThe light of which it spake, all wild beauty,\nAll oldness in new creation:\nAnd though the sweet song be no consolation,\nI cannot wean it from its power be\nIts vileness. I think of her beauty,\nMy heart's life and mine, the love away,\nWhich loves us both forever now: again\nWe shall meet as young men once anew;\nFor long ago to him beautiful\nWas that my heart: let them separate\nWho knew not one another ever.",
